Translate strings to UTF-8 once each in duplicated(), unique() and
anyDuplicated(), and hash strings from their first byte.

When a character vector holds a string in a marked encoding, these
functions hash and compare its strings as UTF-8.  sequal()
(src/main/unique.c) then falls back to Seql(), which calls
translateCharUTF8() on both strings for every probe of the hash table,
so a long latin1 string in a busy probe sequence is translated again
for every lookup that passes it.  shash() also skipped each string's
first byte, so "" and every one-byte string share one hash value and
form one long probe run.

isDuplicated() now caches each element's translation as it adds the
element.  It compares with sequalTr(), which keeps sequal()'s tests on
the original strings and takes only the translated bytes from the
cache, so results do not change.  The cache is allocated only when
some string needs translating.  shash() now hashes from the first
byte.

Found by OSS-Fuzz (libFuzzer_r_sort): testcase 6230127755984896, an
unreproducible Timeout in slot 19 (Encoding(l) <- "latin1"; ...;
unique(l); duplicated(c(l, x))).  The 7 KB input is a 2245-byte line
of mostly 0x90 and 0x96 followed by 1459 empty lines; the long line
hashes into the run of empty and one-byte strings and is translated
for each of their lookups.  R 4.6.1 takes 0.25 s in unique(l) and
0.48 s in duplicated(c(l, x)); under ASan each translation's buffer
allocation pushed the slot past 25 s.  With this patch both take
about 1 ms.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #499, filed 2026-11-16; no R
Bugzilla report yet.  The upstream PR also adds a regression test to
tests/reg-fuzz.R, left out here so this carry patch does not go stale
with that file.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

